[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. The reports in it say
otherwise. Read by tenant and by body, not by subject line or intake tag, they describe three
problems. Each has its own fix, so each now has its own ticket.

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix closes only the first ticket. The other two keep coming in after it ships.
</Callout>

## The three problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads dates month first.** Every tenant writes the day first, so
day and month swap: a booking for 7 April goes out as 4 July. This covers app and email reports,
and form reports from `booking-v2` tenants, whose hint is already `DD/MM/YYYY`.

**`hint`: `booking-v3` tells day-first people to type the month first.** Its date field prints
`MM/DD/YYYY`, people follow it, and the form reads the field the tenant's way. The result looks
like the parser bug, but a parser fix does not touch it. These are the form reports from
`booking-v3` tenants. The cause table on #4471 already marks them "no ticket of its own".

**`shift`: some dates move by one day, not by a swap.** Tuesday shows as Monday, Lisbon gets
Tuesday and Toronto gets Monday, an invite arrives before the booking was made. A month-first
parser cannot move a date by one day. This looks like a date stored as midnight and shown in
another time zone. The desk already lists these reports in `desk-notes.json` as a one-day move,
but #4471's table files them under `parser` by tenant.

## How the counts are made

- One id, one report: the export pages overlap, so repeated rows are dropped first.
- `parser` and `hint` come from `causeOf()` in `causes.ts`: the tenant's locale and form, and the
  report's channel.
- `shift` is the desk's one-day-move list. Those reports are taken out before the causes are counted.
- The intake tag is shown but never used. It is a guess from the reporter's browser, and it names
  the wrong cause for the share counted under the table.

## Why they were merged

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges reports whose subject lines match.
All three problems produce the same subjects ("Wrong day on the invite", "Date is wrong"), so
subject matching put them in one ticket. The same subject is not the same cause: the
[triage page](/kb/triage/dedupe) shows the pairs.

